#
# The example Wi-Fi HAL reads the platform's persist.vendor.debug.wifi.*
# properties when it starts, as the AOSP HAL does on every device, and the
# platform policy gives its domain no read of that namespace. An unset debug
# property reads as its default, so the HAL behaves the same either way; the
# read is a plain get_prop of a vendor-public type and nothing here lets the
# HAL set it. Without the rule every boot logs a denial.
get_prop(hal_wifi_default, persist_vendor_debug_wifi_prop)
